No touchscreen probe was attempted. The known-good effective configuration explicitly has CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_ATMEL_MXT=n and CONFIG_REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE=n; source checkpoint remains dcbe3781a3b686a48a7f437051d6738689e8a3e7, with no pending source edits. No firmware/configuration upload or always-on touch workaround was added. L6/display votes were not changed.

Static comparison, not a hardware damage claim:
- Upstream Linux 4fecfe9561a33db1320482d5fffb03ce1d8dd7ec drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts.c:3255-3314 documents VDDA=2.57..3.47V and VDD=1.71..3.47V, obtains named supplies, asserts RESET, enables regulators, waits, then releases RESET. It does not program regulator voltages in this probe path.
- The draft board maps vdda to L6, whose inherited constraints are fixed at1.8V (msm8939-pm8916.dtsi:93-95), and maps vdd to the GPIO78 fixed regulator. Its GPIO9/GPIO78 voltage values and vin-supply cascade are not established electrical facts.
- Exact public downstream source candidate 6bf677fd534bae9b720a65c18b6096d2a552e71c, drivers/input/touchscreen/atmel_mxt_ts_336t.c:5547-5575 enables power_ldo GPIO9 before power_ts GPIO78. Its error/remove paths:5698-5716 and5735-5739 disable GPIO9 before GPIO78.
- The invented fixed-regulator cascade encodes the opposite child-before-parent shutdown. Upstream regulator core disables the current output at drivers/regulator/core.c:3280 and then its supply at3304-3305. That sequence and the analog/digital mapping have not been justified for this board.

The parent explicitly directed holding the probe rather than adding an always-on workaround to bypass the unresolved shutdown path. This is an evidence/model/safety gate, not a failed upstream maXTouch-driver test. A future successful tap still would not establish the disputed rail topology.
